              ":question/id": "6624681a-bb00-59db-8df9-4d5a3cd00434",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3627",
              ":question/problem": "Given that $y=5\\ln x$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( \\ln x \\right)= \\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}   & = \\left(5\\ln x\\right)'\\\\\n                                                    & = 5 (\\ln x)'\\\\\n                                                    &=5\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{x}\\\\\n                                                    &= \\dfrac{5}{x}.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t  \n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186096614,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186096414,
              ":question/id": "58d47fb0-cf75-58c4-8eea-f3ae97333159",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3628",
              ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=2\\ln x+x^2-1$, find $f'(x).$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\t\t\tf'(x) &= \\left(2\\ln x+x^2-1\\right)'\\\\\n\t\t\t&=2 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{x}+2x-0\\\\\n\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{2}{x}+2x.\n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "83ce3c28-857b-5538-b362-cf52526e3688",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Differentiating a Sum Containing a Natural Logarithm Function"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186096615,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186096415,
              ":question/id": "f61ac550-d62c-558f-b6d5-0d4c9aba8089",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3629",
              ":question/problem": "Given that $y=4\\log_3 x,$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we apply our formula for the derivative when the base of the logarithm is a number other than $e.$ By doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\t\t\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}&=\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(4\\log_3 x\\right)\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\log_3 x\\right)\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{x \\ln 3}\\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{4}{x \\ln 3}.\n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186096616,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186096416,
              ":question/id": "5eaa00f8-0fd0-5de6-a7c0-965db6de3a5c",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3630",
              ":question/problem": "Given that $y= \\log_4 x + \\ln x$,  find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( \\log_4 x + \\ln x \\right)\\\\\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\log_4 x) + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\ln x )\\\\\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 4} + \\dfrac{1}{x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"
          }
        ],
